WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.240
You know that the best way to prevent the
spread of coronavirus is to wash your hands.

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:07.649
Wash your hands, doo doo, doo doo, doo doo.

00:00:07.649 --> 00:00:09.290
Wash your hands!

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:10.290
But … why?

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:15.530
It’s because soap — regular soap, fancy
honeysuckle soap, artisan peppermint soap,

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:20.180
just any soap — absolutely annihilates viruses
like the coronavirus.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:22.540
Here’s how.

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:25.340
This is what a virus, like coronavirus, looks
like.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:30.880
It’s a bit of material surrounded by a coating
of proteins — and fat.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:35.690
Viruses easily stick to places like your hands,
but when you rinse your hands with just water,

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:37.510
it rushes right over the virus.

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:43.120
That’s because that layer of fat makes the
virus behave kind of like a drop of oil.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:45.690
You can see it happening in this demonstration.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:47.750
Oils are just liquid fats.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:51.030
What happens when you pour oil into water?

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:55.260
It floats — it doesn’t mix.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:01:00.820
But add soap…

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:05.160
And suddenly that fatty oil dissolves into
the water.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:09.540
That’s because inside, soap has two-sided
molecules.

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:13.920
One end of the molecule is attracted to water,
the other end to fat.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:18.570
So when the soap molecules come in contact
with water and fat, these dual attractions

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:23.070
literally pull the fat apart, surrounding
the oil particles and dispersing them through the water.

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:24.070
 

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:26.140
Let’s go back to our coronavirus molecule.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:28.890
With that layer of fat holding everything
together.

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:30.340
When it interacts with soap … bam!

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:33.909
The fat gets pulled out by the soap.

00:01:33.909 --> 00:01:38.200
Soap literally pulls apart and demolishes
these viruses.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:42.880
And then the water rinses the harmless, leftover
shards of virus down the drain.

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:47.960
But, and you know where I'm going with this, it takes time for this effect to happen.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:51.400
20 seconds, to be specific.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:55.540
To show why, we ordered this lotion that mimics
viruses and their fatty layers.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:02:00.560
It glows under a UV light.

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:05.590
If you just rinse your hands under regular
water … nothing comes off.

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:11.370
If you wash for just 5 seconds or 10 seconds,
your hands are still covered.

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:15.750
The virus is still here, able to get you and
others sick.

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:18.180
But 20 full seconds:

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:22.660
Now the soap is actually
destroying the virus.

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:27.720
Hand sanitizer works too, because it’s mostly
alcohol, and alcohol works in a somewhat similar

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:31.230
way to soap, breaking down that fatty layer.

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:34.650
You need a high concentration of alcohol to
make that work.

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:39.310
The CDC recommends hand sanitizers with at
least 60% alcohol.

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:44.470
But even with 60% alcohol, the CDC recommends
using soap if you can.

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:49.099
If your hands are sweaty or dirty when you
use the sanitizer, that can dilute it and

00:02:49.099 --> 00:02:51.599
diminish its effectiveness.

00:02:51.599 --> 00:02:54.099
As for soap, just any old soap works.

00:02:54.099 --> 00:02:57.730
You don’t need soap marketed as antibacterial,
even.

00:02:57.730 --> 00:03:01.780
The FDA says skip it — there’s no proof
it is any more effective.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:03.290
Just be sure to wash your hands.

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:05.660
For 20 seconds.

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:10.390
That’s “Happy Birthday” twice.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:14.060
Or the chorus to Lizzo’s “Truth Hurts.”

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.420
Or Prince.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:18.490
Or Eminem.

00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:21.090
Or even Dolly.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:25.050
Just as long as it’s 20 seconds.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.960
And you’re using the ultimate virus annihilator:
soap.

